    "q-236399": {
      "dom_id": "step-q236399",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Given the arithmetic sequence ${a}_{n}=100-8n$ for $n\\ge 1,$ the index of the term $-620$ is\n\n$n=$\n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence, we solve for the value of $n$ that gives ${a}_{n}=-620$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =100-8n \\\\ -620 & =100-8n \\\\ 8n & =720 \\\\ n & =90\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $-620$ is the $90$th term of the sequence.",
