    "q-214192": {
      "dom_id": "step-q214192",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Given the arithmetic sequence ${a}_{n}=3n-4$ for $n\\ge 1,$ the index of the term $146$ is\n\n$n=$\n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence, we solve for the value of $n$ that gives ${a}_{n}=146$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =3n-4 \\\\ 146 & =3n-4 \\\\ 150 & =3n \\\\ 50 & =n \\\\ n & =50\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $146$ is the $50$th term of the sequence.",
