    "q-101056": {
      "dom_id": "step-q101056",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "What is the index of the term $24$ for the arithmetic sequence below?\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+2,\\,{a}_{1}=-8,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "We will convert the recursive formula to an explicit formula and then solve for the value of $n$ such that ${a}_{n}=24.$\n\nThe recursive rule for an arithmetic sequence takes the form\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+d.\n$$\n\nIn the given formula, we have $d=2.$ We are also told that ${a}_{1}=-8,$ so we can write the explicit formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =-8+(n-1)(2) \\\\  & =-8+2n-2 \\\\  & =2n-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for the value of $n$ such that ${a}_{n}=24:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =2n-10 \\\\ 24 & =2n-10 \\\\ 34 & =2n \\\\ \\frac{34}{2} & =n \\\\ 17 & =n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $24$ is the $17$th term of the sequence.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
