    "q-236074": {
      "dom_id": "step-q236074",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Given an arithmetic sequence that has $f(11)=78$ and common difference $d=4$, what is the index of the term $50?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $f(11)=78$ is $10$ jumps after $f(1),$ we can determine the first term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(11) & =f(1)+10d \\\\ 78 & =f(1)+10(4) \\\\ 78 & =f(1)+40 \\\\ 38 & =f(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the formula for the $n$th term is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n) & =f(1)+(n-1)d \\\\  & =38+(n-1)(4) \\\\  & =38+4n-4 \\\\  & =4n+34\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for the value of $n$ that gives $f(n)=50,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n) & =4n+34 \\\\ 50 & =4n+34 \\\\ 16 & =4n \\\\ \\frac{16}{4} & =n \\\\ 4 & =n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $50$ is the $4$th term of the sequence.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-236074-a",
